{"id": "sevt_01YBxKZpRH1zzabGa2AxR4tv", "content": [{"text": "**Evidence**\n- The checkout deploy `0860430` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\") went out at 14:09:42. Checkout p99 went from about 75 ms at 14:08 to 2090 ms at 14:09, then 3965 ms at 14:10. It kept climbing to about 6200 ms by 14:59. The gap between deploy and spike is under a minute.\n- The auth deploy (10:47) and the cart deploy (14:33) don't fit. The spike was already underway before the cart deploy.\n- The diff replaces one batched `order_items WHERE order_id IN (...)` query, grouped in memory, with a query per order inside a loop. That is the N+1 pattern the runbook lists first.\n- The log shows 5,434 `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` queries from checkout. The first appears at 14:09:47, five seconds after the deploy. Many of them come from the same request (`req_efdbfa38dfed`), at about 16\u201324 ms each, so latency grows with the number of orders in a request.\n- I did not check `db_pool_utilization`. The deploy lined up, so the runbook doesn't call for it.\n\n**Fix:** revert `0860430`, or restore the batched query and keep the readable loop.\n\n> **Root cause:** `0860430` \u2014 the refactor replaced the single batched `order_items` query with one query per order row (N+1), so each checkout summary request now makes many sequential DB round-trips.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:45:15.754886Z", "type": "agent.message"}
